pocket-motion-only: a rounded box under a rotation is drawn through MASK_PUSH (0013), this repository's op, which no upstream backend draws; upstream's own backends keep the plain-box degradation for a turned rounded box.

0028 — a turned rounded box keeps its corners.

`emit_rounded_box` drew any rounded box under a world that was not
axis-aligned as the plain box: a turning `rounded-full` circle was a turning
square, and films drew turning circles as images. Under such a world it now
emits the box's AABB as a SCISSOR, the rounded rectangle `mask_outline`
flattens for `overflow-mask` as a MASK_PUSH (0024's sub-pixel outline), the
box's fill, and the two pops. The coverage at the edge is the outline's,
sampled as a mask is. A flat fill is drawn two screen pixels past the box
on every side, so its own edge never multiplies the outline's; a two-stop
gradient keeps its own box so its colours stay the box's, and its straight
edges are the TRI fan's, as a turned square gradient's are. The
axis-aligned path is untouched, so every unturned rounded box is
byte-identical and the ledger is the check.

Guard: `a_turned_rounded_box_keeps_its_corners`
(`engine/core/src/tests.rs`): a 100 px `rounded-full` box turned 30 and 45
degrees has the unturned circle's area (within 1.5 % of pi r^2) and no ink
at 0.9 of the half-diagonal along the square's turned corners; radius 0
turned is still the square. Red before (turned 30: area 9,896, the square),
green after.

Ledgers, against the same tree without this patch: no digest and no
`visibility` row moves — every rounded box in the ledger is unturned, which
is the byte-identity the axis-aligned path owes, and no composition turns
one, so the core test is this change's only guard.

`git apply` skips everything above the first `diff --git`.

